# VTID-04263 — commands log

Investigation, not code generation from a plan file — this session traced a
user-reported "endless failure reports of routines" complaint end to end
across two separate systems (Claude Code Remote Routines and GitHub Actions
scheduled workflows) before making any change.

## Diagnosis (read-only)

- `mcp__Claude_Code_Remote__list_triggers` — inventoried all Routines on the
  account; found 15/16 recurring ones curl a decommissioned GCP Cloud Run
  host (`gateway-q74ibpv6ia-uc.a.run.app`) against a `/api/v1/routines/*`
  API never built server-side. Out of this repo's reach (this session did
  not create those Routines; `update_trigger` was refused by the harness).
- `mcp__github__actions_list` / `get_job_logs` — audited every scheduled
  workflow in exafyltd/vitana-platform and exafyltd/vitana-v1, cross-checked
  against CLAUDE.md's own documented history of dead-GCP-host bugs.
- `mcp__Supabase__execute_sql` (project inmkhvwdcuyhnxkgfvsb, read-only)
  against the five PostgREST RPCs MORNING-SYSTEM-HEALTH-CHECK.yml calls:
    select ci_system_health();
    select ci_welcome_greeting_health();
    select ci_vital_systems_health();
    select ci_orb_session_state_health();
    select ci_ledger_integrity_check(3);
  All five returned healthy — the checks that depend on them (5-12, 16, 17
  in the workflow) are not the source of the 3/21 failures the workflow's
  last scheduled run reported.
- Live curl against every HTTP-based check (1-3, 13-15, 18-19): all 200/ok.
- `git log`/`git diff` comparing the staging build-info commit against the
  latest gateway-touching commit on main: 1 commit behind, 8 minutes old —
  transient auto-deploy lag, not a real defect (check 4).
- `mcp__github__get_job_logs` on ALERT-ORB-SESSION-STATE-HEALTH.yml's two
  most recent runs: both failed on `acks_failed_24h=1` even though the
  underlying RPC data (confirmed above) is healthy — traced to
  `writeOrbSessionState()`'s `reason` field being computed but dropped
  before the OASIS event that the alert reads.
- `mcp__github__get_job_logs` on ALERT-PUSH-DISPATCH-HEALTH.yml (497 total
  runs, most recent + several prior all `failure`): real data —
  `unsent=1000 oldest_age_min=299504`. This workflow is NOT in
  MORNING-SYSTEM-HEALTH-CHECK.yml's check-21 self-audit watchlist, so this
  severe ongoing failure produced no visibility in the daily report.
- `mcp__github__get_job_logs` on CRON-SHADOW-COMPARISON-REPORT.yml,
  EXERCISE-STAGING-SHADOW.yml, EXERCISE-STAGING-SHADOW-CORPUS.yml: the
  first's dead-GCP-URL failure predates VTID-04225's fix (already merged,
  self-resolving on next run). The latter two, run TODAY on the corrected
  URL, both fail with `HTTP 401 {"ok":false,"error":"invalid service
  token"}` — a `GATEWAY_SERVICE_TOKEN` mismatch between AWS Secrets Manager
  and the GitHub repo secret. This session has no `aws` CLI (confirmed:
  `which aws` → command not found) and no access to secret values, so this
  is flagged for an operator, not fixed here.
- `grep -rEo 'q74ibpv6ia-uc\.a\.run\.app|preview\.vitanaland\.com|preview-gateway\.vitanaland\.com|lovable-vitana-vers1'`
  over `.github/workflows/` found one remaining live default in
  AWS-STAGING-VALIDATION.yml (workflow_dispatch-only, never auto-fires).

## Fix (code changes)

1. `services/gateway/src/routes/orb-live.ts` — added `reason: r.reason` to
   the `orb.session.audio_ready.acked` OASIS event payload.
2. `.github/workflows/MORNING-SYSTEM-HEALTH-CHECK.yml` — added
   `ALERT-PUSH-DISPATCH-HEALTH.yml` and `ALERT-APP-USERS-IDENTITY-DRIFT.yml`
   to check 21's self-audit WATCHLIST array.
3. `.github/workflows/AWS-STAGING-VALIDATION.yml` — blanked the dead-GCP-URL
   defaults on `gcp_gateway_url`/`gcp_frontend_url`, annotated the workflow
   as dormant GCP-cutover-era scaffolding.

## Verification

```
cd services/gateway && npx tsc --noEmit -p .
# exit 0, 0 errors

cd services/gateway && npm run build
# exit 0 — tsc + copy-frontend + copy-data all succeeded

python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/MORNING-SYSTEM-HEALTH-CHECK.yml')); yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/AWS-STAGING-VALIDATION.yml'))"
# both parse cleanly

git diff origin/main...HEAD -- services/gateway/src/routes/ services/gateway/src/index.ts services/gateway/src/app.ts > /tmp/route_diff.txt
node scripts/ci/validator-path-guard.cjs --route-evidence-required /tmp/route_diff.txt
# "No route registration added — route-mount evidence not required for this diff." (exit 1)
```

## Not done here (flagged for the user / an operator)

- Disable the 15 dead Claude Code Remote Routines — needs the user (this
  session's `update_trigger`/`delete_trigger` calls were refused: they were
  created via `http_api`, not by an agent, and several attempts were also
  independently blocked by the harness's own safety classifier).
- Root-cause and restart the actual push-notification dispatch scheduler
  (AWS EventBridge Scheduler + Lambda `vitana-push-dispatch`, per VTID-03656)
  — no AWS CLI/credentials in this session.
- Resync `GATEWAY_SERVICE_TOKEN` between AWS Secrets Manager and the GitHub
  repo secret for CRON-SHADOW-COMPARISON-REPORT.yml /
  EXERCISE-STAGING-SHADOW*.yml — needs secret-value access this session
  does not have.
